0.$ Recall that an *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nFirst, we compute $A-2I:$\n\n$$\nA-2I=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)v=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)w=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }{{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-2I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "787f9f37-580f-5658-9df9-ce826b611451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472496} {:answer/id #uuid "c4403496-69e1-5d08-b02d-1b03668dd8c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472496} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f1a3fb6-945f-5879-9865-fdc5a922c3f4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473643} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7460c1a4-dd63-595d-8732-ee34d9a2c09a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472498} {:answer/id #uuid "71f5c96a-5c5b-5605-9ce0-b480c9528139" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472498} :answer-field/id #uuid "a767f879-2f51-5809-aebb-daff65b44383" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473644} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a97ed2f-d3d1-546a-874d-42ae2f24fc40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472500} {:answer/id #uuid "be2ff147-060f-5c7b-81e0-38256805dec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472501} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3046741-713a-58b0-a1a8-53bf395bbfbb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473645}] :question/id #uuid "5e5966d3-ce4d-5835-ab91-1f478e587602" :question/math-academy-id "q-109510" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$\n- **II.** $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$\n- **III.** $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{2}$ of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ Recall that an *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nFirst, we compute $A-2I:$\n\n$$\nA-2I=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)w=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{\\,A-2I\\,\\,}{\\to }{{\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{\\,A-2I\\,\\,}{\\to }{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-2I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5a59325-3ce6-5d72-900a-a6549e6f35ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453270} {:answer/id #uuid "63399f97-f600-5b4d-9277-9004f25d5b6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453271} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb03ed9d-b3dd-5132-bfbe-ccb2df04fee2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e287c0dd-d035-550b-872f-c7e895e3bec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453272} {:answer/id #uuid "1b26befe-fc8e-5235-b353-9ac88f6dbda5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453272} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa43db2a-05ff-5509-a48a-142c9a76be13" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454386} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d868348-18f3-58da-a6ed-45e73067cd1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453274} {:answer/id #uuid "3e88ff03-d431-5fab-aefd-9a60f1450262" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453274} :answer-field/id #uuid "78734bd9-b0b4-5000-8278-6ecd43210da2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454387}] :question/id #uuid "93f4dbff-c62f-571f-9c49-e5503854925a" :question/math-academy-id "q-109518" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A$\n\n- **II.** $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A$\n\n- **III.** $v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A$" :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{2}$ of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ Recall that an *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nFirst, we compute $A-I:$\n\n$$\nA-I=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A-I:$\n\n$$\n(A-I)v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A-I:$\n\n$$\n(A-I)w=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A-I\\,}{\\to }{{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A-I\\,}{\\to }{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433717 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18f449b2-97f3-5186-9bd0-39c537f7db13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453258} {:answer/id #uuid "54696726-fb68-57c0-87f4-c1694ab455cd" :answer/type {:db/ident 