sentation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $GHI$ has vertices at $G(5,5),\\,H(-1,-4),$ and $I(3,5).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{G}^{′}{H}^{′}{I}^{′}$, the image of $△GHI$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${G}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{H}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{I}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $△GHI$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $GHI:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 15 & -17 \\\\ 25 & -14 & 21\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{G}^{′}{H}^{′}{I}^{′}$ are ${G}^{′}(-15,25),$\n${H}^{′}(15,-14),$ ${I}^{′}(-17,21).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351277 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b82692e0-ba33-5d1b-aaf9-45e7f08efebd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469230} {:answer/id #uuid "ccaeba5b-a611-504e-9481-73f42eb30de5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469231} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4060c76-fd99-57db-b724-012505e54ad8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470227} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43626a82-4c7d-5839-8b35-5dbd2fbeef2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469232} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b5ad13-8ac3-56be-bb52-c2b04d87d9fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469232} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fc1d35b-4d19-5446-8692-a6461841218a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c12886b2-7831-5eba-a969-677c37d81084" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469234} {:answer/id #uuid "673e6fbe-3530-52f2-8c6b-27a8d45cfa34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469235} :answer-field/id #uuid "b770dba2-847d-5910-b406-9d579c4a6ce4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470229}] :question/id #uuid "e67ff0be-cbbc-585a-82ab-87b00ade6bf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-8125" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-3,0),(3,0),$ and $(0,-3).$ Which of the following are coordinates of a vertex of ${S}^{′}$, the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(21,0)$\n- **II.** $(3,0)$\n- **III.** $(-21,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-21,0),(21,0),(0,3).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394085 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e5878e4-f118-5e48-9f1f-25b06f4e11bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/46/4672e5a5e616c8c6f4d40d1f29a2a8794da4e8d61c8bab09b7483ec292a91410.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394087} {:answer/id #uuid "785d13cd-3fdd-5848-9cdb-db6e373bbb4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0f/0f5bf56cb4e4546079d89fd97b9533676116d4cff5435cbc926b925af5d3f637.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394088} {:answer/id #uuid "9770d4f6-dde0-5f7a-aeb2-5671a5981656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/54/54496f08a7d4d6b5d37713ffe6d4bc903d48da90def0b273c114fb3b27e32bc9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394089} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec43ec3-b120-5bf6-bbac-590a300de61a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3c/3caf43c4c62614f0c38b2f32c12892820ab4ae732669767b0d50104c85eee605.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394090} {:answer/id #uuid "027e492d-1183-5ffe-8e93-74878e08032d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cb/cb590309256b4836583132f707ceb405472d104908f5df45a0d41dfa18c84a30.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3c/3caf43c4c62614f0c38b2f32c12892820ab4ae732669767b0d50104c85eee605.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394090} :answer-field/id #uuid "18abe65c-6c5d-58b2-9bd6-68ded8dd9d89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394086}] :question/id #uuid "620f4a44-3dbc-5f00-8f93-44670447e38b" :question/math-academy-id "q-8093" :question/problem "![](images/36/369dde2e95b52356b71972b8f1103430e0a840d3d0478626dc5a78cba0f51a41.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $ABCD$ is shown above. Which of the following is ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′},$ the image of $ABCD$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 8 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}$ are $(-1,3),(0,6),(0,8),(-1,5)$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/3c/3caf43c4c62614f0c38b2f32c12892820ab4ae732669767b0d50104c85eee605.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab6cbbc-1e72-5772-9d84-fa9f0fc0337a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/da/da33ca932228a276a69524f3e3039823b0559304f14cb7a3f8df9cebbcb31b9a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394149} {:answer/id #uuid "b93111c4-f3a9-5cc7-8244-16a9df21deef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e5/e5765c41f269f4f937626760ba0b09a6915b42b22fe9abeb08211f989b116a28.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394150} {:answer/id #uuid "f3cdfb2b-2519-533e-beda-5300b92f0613" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/7086e734b0e87e8ac8d7b3efe1a61a5eee817228cba6a61c0c9b227328582046.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394151} {:answer/id #uuid "4d25eba1-06e5-51b2-8cb1-f1c33c6716e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/34f78e657a2e986249f0f32ab87da144256566670dbe87071025287cd245084c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394152} {:answer/id #uuid "64b61d80-6e19-54e8-ae6f-2e68b9297e0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/54/548c907226db9cbdc8fb4dd18c74f3a2001ba7d90973c6f433f67b3e6b87fd29.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/54/548c907226db9cbdc8fb4dd18c74f3a2001ba7d90973c6f433f67b3e6b87fd29.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394153} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dcf4fc3-c298-5327-9384-fdadc5f9db61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394148}] :question/id #uuid "5ad0b5a6-8752-53ba-ae89-ffc7b79418db" :question/math-academy-id "q-8126" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7bfcc5c729475256b70211bcf18e94b605e4486790b13794eaa46cce4f6461bb.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(-3,-1),(-4,0),(-2,2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/54/548c907226db9cbdc8fb4dd18c74f3a2001ba7d90973c6f433f67b3e6b87fd29.png)"}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087781 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087608 :question/id #uuid "8b7758b4-e0ec-5872-90d7-1136c9716574" :question/math-academy-id "e-6682" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n![](images/73/73f0065d4d4768a2c3432559702c2db28fefd050194a5bcdfe44ac3e0b736c82.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{AB}$ is shown below. Find $\\overline{A'B'},$ the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](images/2e/2e22400d15abc81150d6d18de591549e81a46bd16ab9e95f10f86bae2125b490.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overline{AB}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/fe/fe82a0c8616e43c9d8db0b2892a145fcabf4cfa17bd3d4e033a1349cd25921ee.png)\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are $A'(1,3)$ and $B'(1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/47/472f8e712f7d695d5ab3593dafbcc0309feb1a6ac80e9e29c4893dc651d20cf7.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "953dfd34-174b-5642-a24d-910adf741ce2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-5,-4)$ and $(6,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084699} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c2d189-8be5-56ab-9693-f5b4063787b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-5, 4)$ and $(5,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 175921860