)$ and $L(0,2).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints $\\overset{―}{{K}^{′}{L}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{KL}$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${K}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,$ and $\\,{L}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{KL}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{KL}:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 0 & 2\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0 & 3\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${K}^{′}(2,3)$ and ${L}^{′}(-2,2).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345318 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e6343e3-3289-5b36-95e9-1940adc3ce13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,1)$ and $(-1,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342628} {:answer/id #uuid "55c56440-9252-57f9-b712-29ba8b0c2afa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-4,-4)$ and $(-1,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342951} {:answer/id #uuid "87655e3c-5bef-5704-b368-3488db2e45f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,-1)$ and $(-4,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343408} {:answer/id #uuid "89a8dc88-9f1c-5d7f-92ec-23272aef2215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,-4)$ and $(1,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343434} {:answer/id #uuid "b93f95f3-a47f-5e25-8dd2-bb184a3e29fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,-4)$ and $(-1,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,-4)$ and $(-1,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343866} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e52d83b-9516-5498-a46e-27aeb99f9913" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344740}] :question/id #uuid "3d22ea12-f870-522c-bdfa-67aa1ff0afb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-77700" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ has endpoints at $A(1,-2)$ and $B(-2,1).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(-1,-4)$ and ${B}^{′}(-1,-1).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345319 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b64b3ba-5a1f-59b9-9512-47cf89f78424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(3,0)$ and $(1,5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342335} {:answer/id #uuid "31a2fbc2-aaee-52c0-98a2-c589766f2771" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,4)$ and $(3,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342657} {:answer/id #uuid "86ea5a61-ba83-5109-8996-780ec0fb2ba9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,4)$ and $(3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343401} {:answer/id #uuid "9dfb5f40-9fae-5d47-87b9-2ccea22a2b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,5)$ and $(3,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343626} {:answer/id #uuid "f4796c8c-a8ec-576e-bca4-59d6572c9a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,5)$ and $(3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,5)$ and $(3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344392} :answer-field/id #uuid "e186ac35-ea31-5b10-8adf-75ed99feb04a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344888}] :question/id #uuid "c61950ea-c845-593a-8e7e-d2278731a780" :question/math-academy-id "q-77702" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ has endpoints at $A(-1,2)$ and $B(1,1).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(0,5)$ and ${B}^{′}(3,1).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "459256bf-b677-52f4-957b-1f0daf9a3138" :answer/type